In the conversation, James asked about replacing rows in a pandas array “in-place” and was provided with several methods including using `iloc`, `loc`, and condition-based replacement. Each method demonstrated how to modify a DataFrame directly without creating a new object. James then inquired about adding a column to a DataFrame without modifying the original. The response outlined two approaches: creating a copy of the DataFrame using the `copy()` method and using the `assign()` method to return a new DataFrame with the additional column. Both methods preserved the original DataFrame, ensuring it remained unchanged.
